      "id": 114980,
      "name": "lynkfox",
      "username": "lynkfox",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-15T23:23:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If you watch the videos on the kickstarte they are some pretty sturdy material. if the pegs are too big a little work with an exacto knife will do the trick. A tiny drop of modeling glue (i like to use the ones with the long wire thin applicator for this kind of work) will seal it up fine. If you do manage to mess up a foot, a tiny bit of flock (fake grass) or some miniature rocks will do a nice trick around it to keep the majority of the base clear for play purposes, and yet still look great</p>",
